refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
final public intstringPDOException::getCode
Returns the exception code. This is the inherited Exception::getCode, but unlike in most other exceptions, the code is usually a string.

  &reftitle.examples;

   PDOException::getCode example


<?php
$pdo = new PDO('sqlite::memory:');

try {
    $pdo->query('SELECT * FROM missing_table');
} catch (PDOException $e) {
    var_dump($e->getCode());
}
?>


   &example.outputs;


string(5) "HY000"




   Rethrowing a PDOException


<?php
class DatabaseException extends RuntimeException {}

$pdo = new PDO('sqlite::memory:');

try {
    try {
        $pdo->query('SELECT * FROM missing_table');
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        // Passing $e->getCode() as the code would throw a TypeError
        throw new DatabaseException('Query failed', previous: $e);
    }
} catch (DatabaseException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), ': ', $e->getPrevious()->getCode(), "\n";
}
?>


   &example.outputs;


Query failed: HY000
